{
 "note": "New Bridgefield (1929-30, built by Gavin Forrest for Elizabeth Higgins; Main Street Historic Walk site 2): the brick house on the corner at the north entrance to the shops, a boarding house until 1989, restored, and an Italian restaurant since 2003 (La Scarpetta Trattoria, with Pizzica downstairs in recent listings). From the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026) and a 2019 street photo. A brick house under a big red hip roof with a north gable in dark timber, a tall chimney, and on the street corner the landmark: a two-tier octagonal pavilion with a red pointed roof, timber posts and a cream frieze, topped by a small cream lantern with its own red cap (drawn square here). Behind a lawn and a white picket fence. Name in plain lettering, no logo. Metres: x left to right as seen from the side street (east to west), y back (south-south-east) from the front of the house.",
